{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \"worker lint|lint debt|Worker A|ab5|worker package|lint:check|typecheck\" /Users/danielpenin/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md'","aggregated_output":"38:- `npm run check:all` passed after the code fixes and remained the strongest local signal that the repo’s main quality/visual/security/typecheck/test gates were back in line [Task 1]\n113:- A strong narrow proof surface for Kloel MIND repairs is the focused backend suite around `brain-commercial-graph`, `mind-*`, `brain-event-spine`, related inbound/channel services, then `npm --prefix backend run typecheck`, `npm --prefix backend run lint:check`, and finally repo-wide `npm run check:all` [Task 2]\n396:- The real stack in this checkout is backend NestJS + Prisma + Postgres/BullMQ/Redis, a main Next.js frontend, a separate `frontend-admin`, and an existing worker package; Phase 0 planning should account for all four surfaces [Task 1]\n766:- rollout_summaries/2026-04-23T23-55-43-lL0s-pr198_accumulated_worktree_green_restore.md (cwd=/Users/danielpenin/whatsapp_saas, rollout_path=/Users/danielpenin/.codex/sessions/2026/04/23/rollout-2026-04-23T20-55-43-019dbcc5-582f-78e1-b419-cf9c675aff80.jsonl, updated_at=2026-04-24T00:23:23+00:00, thread_id=019dbcc5-582f-78e1-b419-cf9c675aff80, got readiness/typechecks green but exposed the broader constructor/spec backlog)\n776:- rollout_summaries/2026-04-24T00-41-38-0Dag-pr_198_accumulated_workspace_stabilization_blocked_by_git_in.md (cwd=/Users/danielpenin/whatsapp_saas, rollout_path=/Users/danielpenin/.codex/sessions/2026/04/23/rollout-2026-04-23T21-41-38-019dbcef-6253-7131-9636-043c969d7ec8.jsonl, updated_at=2026-04-24T02:16:08+00:00, thread_id=019dbcef-6253-7131-9636-043c969d7ec8, fixed targeted fetch/spec issues and brought local architecture diff mode plus backend typecheck back to green)\n777:- rollout_summaries/2026-04-23T23-55-43-lL0s-pr198_accumulated_worktree_green_restore.md (cwd=/Users/danielpenin/whatsapp_saas, rollout_path=/Users/danielpenin/.codex/sessions/2026/04/23/rollout-2026-04-23T20-55-43-019dbcc5-582f-78e1-b419-cf9c675aff80.jsonl, updated_at=2026-04-24T00:23:23+00:00, thread_id=019dbcc5-582f-78e1-b419-cf9c675aff80, showed the wider failing suites and lint debt once readiness/typecheck were fixed)\n852:- The broadest failure cluster after readiness/typecheck recovery was refactor drift, not runtime logic: constructor arity mismatches, stale public controller method names, and outdated spec assumptions around split controllers/services such as `WhatsAppApiController`, `MarketingController.getConnectStatus`, `AuthService`, `CheckoutService`, `PulseService`, `StorageService`, and `CiaRuntimeService` [Task 1][Task 2]\n854:- The safe refactor loop for this branch was: restore broken files from `git show HEAD:<path>`, split one method/file at a time, add explicit context imports/interfaces before extracting private-state-heavy logic, then rerun `npm --prefix backend run typecheck` before touching more files [Task 2]\n861:- `npm run check:all` is the strongest single repo-wide gate for the later Codacy/CI cleanup path too; during the April 29 rollout it passed alongside `backend npm run typecheck`, `backend npm run lint:check -- --max-warnings=0`, `node --check e2e/fake-waha/server.hooks.js`, and `git diff --check` [Task 5]\n869:- The pre-push chain for this repo includes `guard:new-code`, `prisma:validate`, backend typecheck/build/boot smoke, frontend typecheck/tests, and then `frontend:build:clean`; the clean-worktree requirement sits late in the chain, so earlier green steps do not prove the push will land [Task 7]\n936:- `npm run check:all` is the authoritative end-to-end validator for this monorepo. After the fixes and rebase it passed governance-boundary, visual-contract, test-integrity, unsafe-casts, unsafe-queries, security, architecture, layer-boundaries, model-strings, code-quality, data-integrity, ratchet, lint, frontend-typecheck, backend-typecheck, worker-typecheck, frontend-test, backend-test, and worker-test [Task 2]\n1156:- Symptom: onboarding compiles poorly after role-generalization. Cause: `ConnectAccountType` was imported from the wrong module. Fix: import the enum from `@prisma/client` and rerun formatting/typecheck before deeper debugging [Task 2]\n1211:- The focused validation stack that kept recurring for finance work was: targeted Jest suites, then `backend` build/typecheck, then `npm run backend:boot-smoke`, then broader finance regressions. Use that sequence before calling money-path changes stable [Task 1][Task 2]\n1217:- Symptom: a helper extraction or reconnect leaves the frontend broken with `TS2304` missing-symbol errors. Cause: helper file was created but imports or narrowed helper types were not updated. Fix: run `npm --prefix frontend run typecheck` immediately after extraction and patch imports in the same change [Task 3]\n1259:- The pre-push gates that matter for this slice included `guard:changed-eslint`, `guard:test-files`, `guard:visual-contract`, `architecture:check`, `prisma:validate`, `backend:typecheck`, `backend build`, and `backend:boot-smoke` [Task 2]\n1504:- rollout_summaries/2026-04-28T22-47-57-ZlHC-pulse_evidence_autonomy_runtime_proof.md (cwd=/Users/danielpenin/whatsapp_saas, rollout_path=/Users/danielpenin/.codex/sessions/2026/04/28/rollout-2026-04-28T19-47-58-019dd647-1c25-7240-9b19-de04cd33e97c.jsonl, updated_at=2026-04-29T18:36:38+00:00, thread_id=019dd647-1c25-7240-9b19-de04cd33e97c, tightened PULSE-only proof surfaces and validated loader/typecheck changes while deep runtime proof remained incomplete)\n1533:- when the user’s anti-gambiarra prompt is in scope -> prefer automated gates, strict lint/typecheck, and no \"quick fix\" casts or workflow bypasses [Task 2]\n1552:- `frontend/src/app/(main)/chat/page.tsx` is the correct current chat route surface; `frontend/src/app/chat/*` was stale/wrong in that repo state. After route/file moves, clear `frontend/.next` before judging typecheck because stale generated types can reference deleted paths [Task 1]\n1555:- `node scripts/ops/check-all-gates.mjs` became the broad integration check and passed governance-boundary, visual-contract, test-integrity, unsafe-casts, unsafe-queries, security, architecture, layer-boundaries, model-strings, code-quality, data-integrity, ratchet, lint, frontend-typecheck, backend-typecheck, worker-typecheck, and frontend-test before backend-test failed [Task 2]\n1585:- Symptom: PULSE/chat typecheck references deleted routes after route moves. Cause: stale `.next/dev/types`. Fix: remove `frontend/.next`, then rerun typecheck before editing more code [Task 1]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
